#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:185
#. Diagram label
msgid "Computable agreement?"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:198
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Computable only. A person checks that the ODRL says what the text says, and signs it off. A program can check the ODRL is well formed; it cannot check that it matches the text. The check includes the consent duty: present when the legal basis is consent, absent otherwise (consent rule 1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:192
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Computable only. One assigner and one assignee (ODRL 2.2 §2.1.3), permissions and prohibitions with target assets (§2.2), constraints (§2.5.1) and duties (§2.6.3), written as JSON-LD. Purposes from HL7 PurposeOfUse. Consent rule 1: the Agreement carries the odrl:obtainConsent duty only when the legal basis recorded in P1.2a is consent."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:264
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Compute SHA-256 (FIPS 180-4) of the signed text, and of the ODRL file if there is one, recorded as DCAT 3 spdx:checksum and verified by check:dsa-hash."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:421
#. Diagram label
msgid "consent"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:371
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Consent rule 2, for a new version only. `widens use` (for example more data, more purposes, more recipients or a longer period): the Consents that cite the old version do not cover the new one, so new consent is needed. `narrows use`: no new consent is needed. `not consent-based`: there is no consent to renew."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:167
#. Diagram label
msgid "Consent the legal basis?"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:269
#. Diagram label
msgid "Consent-based agreement?"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:276
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Consent-based only. Record the SHA-256 of the plain-language summary beside the agreement's, in the same version (consent rule 3). The summary a person consented to can then be checked against the agreement it summarises; a changed summary is a new version."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:282
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Consent-based only. The version's publication metadata states the fixed-version URL (P2.1) and the hash (P2.2) that a Consent cites in FHIR R4 Consent.policy.uri (consent rule 2), never the 'latest' URL. For a computable agreement that URL is also the ODRL policy uid (P2.3): a Consent counts only when its Consent.policy.uri equals the agreement's ODRL policy uid, so the two are the same string."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:174
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Consent-based only. Write a plain-language summary of the agreement in the same document folio: what it lets the recipient do with the person's data, in words the person can read. Consent rule 3: every agreement that needs consent publishes this summary, hashed with the agreement (P2.2a), and the summary is what the person consents to. It is reviewed, rendered and versioned with the text."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:370
#. Diagram label
msgid "Consent-based: does the amendment widen use?"
msgstr ""

