#. Diagram label
msgid "Terms change, end date reached, or notice given"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:410
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The agreement has expired or been terminated, its catalogue status says so, and its versions stay readable."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:378
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The amendment widens use, so a Consent citing the old version's URL and hash does not cover the new version (consent rule 2). Record on the bean, and in the new version's text, that new consent is needed; the new version gets its own plain-language summary (P1.2b). Asking each person again is the trust layer's."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:53
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The data provider and the data recipient (ODRL 2.2 assigner and assignee) and the people who sign for them. Their role is judgement only: they agree the terms, sign, and decide whether to amend, renew or end the agreement. No skill can make those choices for them, so no activity in this lane names one."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:270
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The legal basis recorded in P1.2a. `consent`: hash the plain-language summary with the agreement, and state the fixed-version URL and hash a Consent cites. `not consent-based`: go straight on."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:300
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The ODRL policy names the signed text distribution with dcterms:source (DCMI Terms), pointing at the immutable URL whose spdx:checksum was just recorded. Its uid is that same fixed-version URL, the URL a Consent cites in Consent.policy.uri (consent rule 2)."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:143
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The parties agree the purpose, the datasets, the period, the conditions and duties, which trust anchors each side accepts, and the legal basis the sharing rests on (consent, treatment, public-health law or a research waiver). This sets what the text must say; it is a negotiation between people."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:348
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The parties decide what happens to the agreement. Deciding to amend or terminate is human; expiry of a computable agreement is already enforced by its ODRL dateTime constraint."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:354
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The parties' decision. `new version` (amend, or renew with a new end date) runs P1 again and publishes a new version linked to the old one. `renew by grant` (the version has no end date): nothing in the document changes. `end` (expiry or termination) closes the agreement."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:240
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The reviewers' call. `changes needed` sends the draft back to the author; `ready` renders it for signing."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:252
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The signatories sign: wet ink, or an electronic signature under national law. Technically a detached JWS (RFC 7515) or CMS (RFC 5652); PAdES for a signed PDF needs the owner's approval."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:324
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The signed version is at its immutable URL, with its hash and catalogue record. Grants and keys that cite it are issued in the server processes (smart-trust), not here."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:162
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The text states the legal basis the parties agreed in P1.1 as a normative statement: consent, treatment, public-health law, or a research waiver. Consent rule 1: only an agreement whose legal basis is consent carries the odrl:obtainConsent duty; treatment, public-health law and research waivers do not rest on consent. The gateway that follows, the ODRL and the reviewers all read the basis from this statement."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:361
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The version has no end date, so renewal is a new grant under the same version. Grants are issued in the server processes (smart-trust), not here."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:422
#. Diagram label
msgid "treatment, law or waiver"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:100
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Used only when the public part of the agreement (the template) goes out for public comment. Comments are handled in Process_PublicComment, the same as for any document folio."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:323
#. Diagram label
msgid "Version published — agreement in force"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:407
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Which outcome the bean was closed with, so each ends at its own named end event. The bean is closed once, on every path (bpmn-authoring: open and close the bean at the top, once)."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:464
#. Diagram label
msgid "widens use"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:156
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Write the agreement as a document folio: one normative statement per clause the parties must keep, through normative-statements. The text says which governs if it and a machine-readable form disagree (suggested: the text)."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/dsa-document-lifecycle.bpmn:68
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Writes the legal text and, for a computable agreement, derives the ODRL 2.2 Agreement from it. Every loop comes back here: a review that asks for changes, an amendment, and a renewal that needs a new version."
msgstr ""

